# A1-P01 — Waking Wrong. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1158–1219.
# Scene: scenes/chapter1/opening_crash_site_hook.tscn. Playable, top-down.
# Kaelen acts because he thinks other passengers might be alive. There is no
# plane, no wreckage and no bodies; the absence is the mystery.
# Each inspect point runs its own node, in any order. "fused_metal" gives the
# route east, which is what lets the player leave.

~ start
Kaelen: Ow. Okay. Ow.
Kaelen (Internal): Still breathing. That's step one done. Step two is standing up, and I'm not ready for step two.
Kaelen: The flight. We were coming down, the cups were going everywhere, and then—
Kaelen: Where's the plane?
do objective Find the plane. Look for survivors.

# The first time the player walks toward the crater's centre.
~ call_out
Kaelen: Hello? Can anyone hear me?
Kaelen: Flight 707! Anyone from 707! Shout, bang on something, and I'll come to you!
Kaelen (Internal): No alarm. No voice. Nobody shouting back, not even to tell me to keep it down. Just wind.

~ scorched_ground
Kaelen: Scorch marks. And no fuel smell, none, after a whole plane came down.
Kaelen (Internal): It should be fuel and burnt plastic for a mile. Instead it smells like rain on somebody's garden.

~ fused_metal
Kaelen: That's metal. That's aircraft metal, it has to be. That's a piece of the plane...
Kaelen: I think it's ours. I can't even tell which part it was.
do translation_flicker
System: SYSTEM TRACE: RECOVERY SECTOR 04-A.
System: SYSTEM TRACE: LOCAL SETTLEMENT ROUTE — EAST.
do runes_return
Kaelen: That was text. Floating over the metal, like a debug label. Somebody tell me I didn't see that.
Kaelen (Internal): Okay. Either I hit my head harder than I think, or something just gave me directions.
Kaelen (Internal): East, then. If anyone else walked out of here, that's the way they'd have gone.
set ch1_crash_trace_seen
do objective Find people. A settlement east may know what happened to Flight 707.

~ safety_card
Kaelen: A safety card. "In the unlikely event of a water landing—" I never once read one of these to the end.
Kaelen: The rest is gone. All that's left is the number in the corner.
Kaelen (Internal): 707. So it wasn't a bad dream on a long flight. It happened, and I was on it.
set ch1_flight_fragment_found

~ seat_marks
Kaelen: That's a row. That's where a row was. You can see where the feet were bolted down.
Kaelen: Somebody sat here. Somebody had the window, and somebody had the aisle. Where are they?
Kaelen: There were people here. Step one: find one person. Just one, and then the next one.

~ sky
Kaelen: The clouds are moving two different ways at once.
Kaelen: Clouds don't do that. They don't— no. Not the clouds. People first.

~ perimeter
Kaelen: A bag. A shoe. Somebody's phone. Anything with a name on it.
Kaelen: Come on. Nobody gets off a plane with nothing. Somebody had to drop something...

# The player reaches the east road after finding the trace.
~ leave
do sfx distant_cry
Kaelen (Internal): Whatever made that noise, it isn't one of ours. People don't sound like that, not even hurt.
Kaelen (Internal): East. Keep moving east, faster than I want to.

# The player tries to leave before finding the trace.
~ leave_blocked
Kaelen (Internal): Not until I know which way they'd have gone. I'm not leaving anyone behind on a guess.
